"""Revised ESG classification rules (classifier v1.0).

Each rule: (rule_id, kind, topic, pillar, pattern, confidence, rationale, paper_keywords)
Rules are applied IN ORDER to the normalized metricOther text; every match CONSUMES its span so that
later, more generic rules cannot re-use it (e.g. 'product safety' is routed to Extended before the
generic 'safety' rule runs; 'safety and soundness' is masked before it).

kind
  MASK      span neutralised, no evidence (company / segment / product names, homonyms)
  MASKN     span neutralised AND counted as non-ESG evidence (e.g. 'safety and soundness', 'economic environment')
  ESG       Strict ESG evidence (pillar E / S / G, or GEN = multi-pillar ESG/CSR/sustainability)
  EXT       Extended-only stakeholder evidence (customers, product responsibility, community engagement,
            customer-facing service reliability); never Strict
  EXT_AMB   stakeholder meaning possible but unclear -> Strict 0, Extended Unknown
  AMB       ESG meaning possible but unclear -> Strict Unknown (and Extended Unknown)
  ADJ       ESG-adjacent but excluded by definition (generic compliance/risk/controls/cyber, generic
            workforce/talent/succession, renewable-energy business-line execution) -> 0/0 + flag
  NONESG    informative non-ESG content (financial, market, operating, product-development ...)
  NONSPEC   non-specific placeholder (individual / strategic / discretionary ...) -> Unknown
Decision precedence: ESG > AMB > NONSPEC > (EXT | EXT_AMB | ADJ | NONESG) > nothing matched (Unknown).
"""

R = []
def add(kind, topic, pillar, pattern, conf="high", why="", kw=""):
    R.append(dict(kind=kind, topic=topic, pillar=pillar, pattern=pattern, confidence=conf, rationale=why, paper_keywords=kw))

